<.shell title="Empty state" current={:empty_state}>
  <h1>Empty state</h1>
  <p class="lead">Why a list is empty and what to do.</p>

  <div class="example">
    <.empty_state title="No groups yet">
      SAR Duty copies groups from D4H when it refreshes.
      <:action><.button size={:sm}>Refresh from D4H</.button></:action>
    </.empty_state>
  </div>

  <h2>When to use</h2>
  <p>
    In place of a page's main list when it has no rows, such as groups, qualifications, or
    proposed changes.
  </p>

  <h2>When not to use</h2>
  <p>A short list inside a page, such as a member's groups. A sentence is enough.</p>

  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <p>
    The title says what is missing. The text says why, and what to do. Not only "No results". An
    action, when there is one, goes under it.
  </p>

  <h2>In the app</h2>
  <p>
    <code>&lt;.empty_state title="No groups yet"&gt;</code>, with the reason inside and an optional
    <code>&lt;:action&gt;</code>. Show it instead of the table, not under an empty one.
  </p>
</.shell>
